  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Prime stretch of Fall weather is in the late \ninnings with rain and breezy conditions forecast Sunday from \nIsaias\n\nThe ongoing string of dry and comfortable Fall days and crisp,\ncool Autumn nights will come to an end on Sunday as rain and \nbreezy conditions arrive from Isaias. \n\nWe can't rule out some patchy frost across the usually colder\nvalley spots in the NW Alleghenies and Laurel Highlands \ntonight.\n\nRainfall timing continues to focus during the day on Sunday\nbefore tapering off Sunday night into early Monday/Columbus Day.\nTotal rainfall amounts are generally forecast in the 0.50-1.50\ninch range over a 24-36hr duration with a low risk of potential\nflooding impacts. Wind gusts 35-40 mph are possible over the \nridgetops in the Laurel Highlands on Sunday.",
